# OORT_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS: This is a comma-separated list of allowed origins for CORS requests. If none are specified, 
# there will be a strict single origin policy in place for the whole app. This is the most secure 
# configuration, but is not suitable for all use cases. Use a comma separated, if there are specific domains that you want to allow. (E.g., 'https://example.com,https://another-example.com') Setting to '*' will allow all origins, which is the most insecure settings, but is suitable in limited use cases, such as open APIs. Consider using the more specific @cross_origin decorator if you want to enable cross origin requests on specific routes. 
